# 02 — Render Pipeline (R3F Revision)

## 1. Overview

With R3F, the render pipeline becomes declarative. Layers are R3F components that manage Three.js objects through React's lifecycle. R3F handles disposal, frame scheduling, and canvas management.

```
Viewport3DRenderModel
       │
       ▼
  <Canvas frameloop="demand">
       │
       ├── <MeshSurfaceLayer />      (topology surface)
       ├── <ScalarFieldLayer />      (vertex colors from field)
       ├── <VectorGlyphLayer />      (instanced arrows)
       ├── <WireframeLayer />        (edge overlay)
       ├── <SelectionLayer />        (outline/tint)
       ├── <AxesGridLayer />         (axes + grid)
       ├── <AirboxLayer />           (domain boundary wireframe)
       └── <ClipPlaneLayer />        (clipping plane + cap)
```

## 2. R3F Canvas Setup

```tsx
function ViewportPane({ config, renderModel }: Props) {
  return (
    <Canvas
      frameloop="demand"          // ← no continuous rendering
      gl={{ antialias: true, alpha: false, powerPreference: "high-performance" }}
      camera={{ fov: 45, near: 0.1, far: 10000 }}
      onCreated={({ gl }) => {
        gl.toneMapping = THREE.NoToneMapping;
      }}
    >
      <SyncedOrbitControls />
      <SceneLighting displayMode={config.displayMode} />

      {config.layers.meshSurface && (
        <MeshSurfaceLayer topology={renderModel.topology} mode={config.displayMode} />
      )}
      {config.layers.scalarField && renderModel.scalarField && (
        <ScalarFieldLayer field={renderModel.scalarField} topology={renderModel.topology} />
      )}
      {/* ...more layers... */}
    </Canvas>
  );
}
```

### Dirty Rendering

R3F's `frameloop="demand"` means:
- No frame rendered unless `invalidate()` is called
- Layer components call `invalidate()` via `useThree()` when their props change
- Camera controls call `invalidate()` on interaction
- **Zero frames when idle** — the spec requirement is met by default

## 3. Layer Components

### MeshSurfaceLayer

```tsx
function MeshSurfaceLayer({ topology, mode }: {
  topology: TopologyRenderData | null;
  mode: DisplayMode;
}) {
  const geometryRef = useRef<THREE.BufferGeometry>(null);
  const { invalidate } = useThree();

  // Update geometry when topology revision changes
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!topology || !geometryRef.current) return;
    const geo = geometryRef.current;
    geo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(topology.positions, 3));
    if (topology.indices) geo.setIndex(new THREE.Uint32BufferAttribute(topology.indices, 1));
    if (topology.normals) geo.setAttribute("normal", new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(topology.normals, 3));
    geo.computeBoundingSphere();
    invalidate();
  }, [topology?.topologyRevision, invalidate]);

  if (!topology) return null;

  return (
    <mesh>
      <bufferGeometry ref={geometryRef} />
      <meshStandardMaterial
        wireframe={mode === "wireframe"}
        flatShading={mode === "flat-shaded"}
        side={THREE.DoubleSide}
      />
    </mesh>
  );
}
```

**Key:** Geometry is updated via imperative `useEffect` keyed on `topologyRevision`. R3F handles disposal of the old geometry when the component unmounts.

### ScalarFieldLayer

```tsx
function ScalarFieldLayer({ field, topology }: {
  field: ScalarFieldRenderData;
  topology: TopologyRenderData | null;
}) {
  const meshRef = useRef<THREE.Mesh>(null);
  const { invalidate } = useThree();

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!meshRef.current || !topology) return;
    const geo = meshRef.current.geometry;
    const colors = colormapValues(field.values, field.min, field.max, field.colorMapName);
    geo.setAttribute("color", new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(colors, 3));
    invalidate();
  }, [field.fieldRevision, invalidate]);

  // ... renders mesh with vertexColors: true
}
```

**Critical rule preserved:** quantity switch updates color attribute, not geometry. `topology.topologyRevision` doesn't change → no geometry rebuild.

### VectorGlyphLayer

```tsx
function VectorGlyphLayer({ vectors }: { vectors: VectorFieldRenderData | null }) {
  const meshRef = useRef<THREE.InstancedMesh>(null);
  const { invalidate } = useThree();

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!vectors || !meshRef.current) return;
    const mesh = meshRef.current;
    // Update instance matrices from positions + directions + magnitudes
    updateInstanceMatrices(mesh, vectors);
    mesh.count = vectors.sampledCount;
    mesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;
    invalidate();
  }, [vectors?.fieldRevision, invalidate]);

  if (!vectors) return null;

  return (
    <instancedMesh ref={meshRef} args={[undefined, undefined, vectors.sampledCount]}>
      <coneGeometry args={[0.3, 1, 8]} />
      <meshStandardMaterial />
    </instancedMesh>
  );
}
```

### AirboxLayer

```tsx
function AirboxLayer({ bounds }: { bounds: Bounds3 | null }) {
  if (!bounds) return null;
  const size = bounds.max.map((v, i) => v - bounds.min[i]) as [number, number, number];
  const center = bounds.min.map((v, i) => v + size[i] / 2) as [number, number, number];

  return (
    <lineSegments position={center}>
      <edgesGeometry args={[new THREE.BoxGeometry(...size)]} />
      <lineBasicMaterial color="#4c9eff" opacity={0.5} transparent />
    </lineSegments>
  );
}
```

## 4. Disposal

R3F handles Three.js resource disposal automatically:
- When a layer component unmounts, its geometries, materials, and textures are disposed
- When the `<Canvas>` unmounts, the WebGL context and all resources are released
- `instancedMesh` instance buffers are cleaned up on unmount

**Non-R3F resources** (workers, large CPU-side typed arrays, object URLs) still need manual cleanup via `useEffect` return functions.

## 5. Display Modes

| Mode | R3F implementation |
|---|---|
| `shaded` | `<meshStandardMaterial />` with 3-point lighting |
| `wireframe` | `<meshBasicMaterial wireframe />` |
| `shaded+wireframe` | Two `<mesh>`: standard + wireframe overlay with `depthTest` offset |
| `flat-shaded` | `<meshStandardMaterial flatShading />` |
| `points` | `<points>` with `<pointsMaterial />` |

Display mode is a prop on `MeshSurfaceLayer`. Changing mode swaps the material — no geometry rebuild.

## 6. Lighting

```tsx
function SceneLighting({ displayMode }: { displayMode: DisplayMode }) {
  if (displayMode === "wireframe" || displayMode === "points") return null;

  return (
    <>
      <ambientLight intensity={0.4} />
      <directionalLight position={[10, 10, 10]} intensity={0.6} />
      <directionalLight position={[-5, 5, -5]} intensity={0.3} />
    </>
  );
}
```

## 7. Context Loss

R3F handles WebGL context loss/recovery internally. The `<Canvas>` component catches `webglcontextlost`, prevents default, and rebuilds on `webglcontextrestored`. All declarative scene objects are recreated from the current React tree — no manual recovery needed.
